  m_Name: Pierogi
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::IngredientData
  _name: Pierogi
  _spoilTime: 15
  _normalSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 668a264a6ce95d24e969eec737f87ad6, type: 3}
  _spoiledSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 8d895d7cf5f85da46bec09c5d1cf53ea, type: 3}
  _plateSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 427cc329f07795841825c0878a64a6a0, type: 3}
  _isSmallIngredient: 0
  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: "<i>A Doctor\u2019s Journal: Day 45</i>\r\n\r\n<i>11:46
    AM: One of my patients recently introduced me to this dumpling from the Island
    Confederacy. The use of baked potatoes and white cattle\u2019s cheese makes it
    evident it has used the Western style of grilling. The whole world is taking
    inspiration from Verehn. What a curious loop of teachers and students. Anyways.
    I have my beliefs on this hand food being a lead into this \u201CSpoilage\u201D
    epidemic. The western nation recently experienced a social revolution a few years
    back before our own. The breakdown of fodder logistics starved the nation\u2019s
    cattle and the people of its cheese. I have my hypothesis that expired foodstuffs
    correlate with the black Spoilage our own people are suffering from. I will conduct
    single-blind studies with some of my subjects for the next few days.</i>\r\n"
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: "<i>A Doctor\u2019s Journal: Day 49</i>\n<i>3:14
    AM: I have done it! I have found a correlation between feeding fresh cheese in
    pierogi and a heightened aggression from my double-headed subject. I left some
    white cheese out the fridge for a few moments and almost immediately began releasing
    black goo. I added this cheese to some pierogi, western-grilled, became almost
    pitch black in color, and fed it to one of my subject\u2019s heads. I recorded
    no substantial change in behavior, except a statement from the head which stated
    to be \u201Cchewy, yet not regretful\u201D. In fact, I am surprised to see that
    upon feeding the other head some fresh white cheese, the head began to scream
    erratically. Truly fascinating!\r\n\rThe mass of fresh cheese can directly aggravate
    one of the heads of my subject. Is it from the cheese\u2019s contents, or from
    mental stress from its taste?  I am certain this will lead me toward a cure sooner
    than later.\r\n\r\n7:23 AM: I must report that my subject has escaped my facility,
    noted by the Y-shaped hole in its tent. I must also state that I woke up with
    the taste of cheese in my mouth. The case is under investigation. I am currently
    in an agitated state as of writing this. This is an opportunity I shall not pass
    and will write down my progress as the days follow.</i>"
